# Canvas Rendering Rules

- **PixiJS v8** plus `pixi-box-shadow` own the visual output. Grid and component layers live under `src/canvas/` (`grid/setup.ts`, `components/componentLayer.ts`, type builders under `components/<type>/`, `selection-setup.ts`) and subscribe to **`src/store.ts`**.
- **`src/canvas/index.tsx`** composes `<Pixi>` (from `src/components/pixi/`) and DOM pointer handlers; **`src/components/pixi/index.tsx`** runs `Application` init once and resizes on logical size changes. Optional **`onPreload`** runs before `Application.init` / tickers / first render — **`GridCanvas`** passes **`preloadIconBoxTitleFont`** so icon-box Canvas `Text` uses the **`@font-face`** in `App.css` (`src/fonts/iconBoxTitle.ts`).
- Keep drawing deterministic from store state: **`grid`**, **`instances`**, **`selectedInstanceId`**, drag preview on **`dragState`**.
- Name coordinate spaces clearly: logical/model coordinates, CSS pixels, and backing-store pixels (`devicePixelRatio`) are different.
- Hit testing stays in `src/canvas/hitTest.ts` (registry bounds + top-most order). Pointer code maps DOM coordinates to logical space from the `.canvas-shell` bounds.
- **Viewport**: pan + zoom are **`canvasPan` / `canvasZoom`** on **`.canvas-shell`** only. **`.canvas-panel-scroll`** does not use native overflow scroll (avoids fighting transform). Wheel on the **`<canvas>`**: unmodified = pan; ⌘/Ctrl = zoom; layer drag edge auto-pan uses **`translateCanvasPan`**, not `scrollLeft`.
- **PNG copy** uses **`app.renderer.extract.image`** at **resolution `2`**; clear selection before extract; **`copyDocumentPng()`** reads **`pixiApp`** from the global store.
